#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
SYNTAX World Bank Interim Audit System

Fiduciary review of Interim Unaudited Financial Reports (IFRs) submitted by
borrowers on Bank-financed projects, plus the procurement and counterparty
checks that sit alongside them.

Covers:
    IFR submission timeliness against the reporting covenant
    Designated Account reconciliation (opening + advances - uses = closing)
    Disbursement category allocation, eligibility, and financing percentage
    Forecast-to-actual variance against tolerance
    Statement of Expenditures (SOE) ceiling use
    Procurement prior-review thresholds and contract splitting
    Debarred and cross-debarred counterparties
    Annual audit opinion modifications

Findings roll up into an FM risk rating and, where a fiduciary condition also
indicates evasion, cross into the SANCTIONS module as evasion signals.

IMPORTANT - thresholds, tolerances, and submission windows below are a
structural model carrying representative values, not an authoritative
transcription of any Financing Agreement or Bank procedure. Project-specific
covenants govern; validate AUDIT_PARAMETERS and every project's own category
table against the applicable legal agreement before operational use. The system
reports where a report looks internally inconsistent or covenant-divergent; it
does not determine that any borrower, supplier, or person has done anything
wrong. All sample data shipped with --demo is synthetic.

Copyright 2025 - Apache License 2.0
"""

